# SECTION 08 — AI EMAIL MANAGER INTEGRATION

**Existing route:** `/admin/master/email`

The fundraising system must integrate directly with the existing enterprise Email Manager.

Do not duplicate the mailbox system.

## 8.1 Organizational Mailboxes

Support the five reported organizational mailboxes:

- info@phumulani.org
- donations@phumulani.org
- grants@phumulani.org
- executive@phumulani.org
- partnerships@phumulani.org

Verify actual provider connectivity and mailbox authorization before marking any mailbox LIVE.

## 8.2 Unified Communications

Fundraising personnel must be able to:

- View authorized donor correspondence.
- Search conversations.
- Filter by donor.
- Filter by organization.
- Filter by campaign.
- Filter by grant.
- View message history.
- Assign relationship owners.
- Create follow-up tasks.
- Prepare AI response drafts.
- Submit drafts for approval.
- Send approved correspondence.
- Track provider delivery status.

## 8.3 Incoming Email Intelligence

When a donor email arrives:

1. Validate the message.
2. Apply security and safeguarding screening.
3. Identify an existing donor record where permitted.
4. Classify the correspondence.
5. Assign operational priority.
6. Extract documented requests.
7. Identify relevant funding opportunities.
8. Create or update CRM tasks.
9. Generate a response draft when allowed.
10. Request human approval.
11. Send only after authorization.
12. Update the communication timeline.
13. Record an audit event.

## 8.4 Priority Classification

Support P0 through P4.

P0 safeguarding matters require immediate restricted human escalation and must bypass general fundraising AI.

Fundraising priority must never override safeguarding controls.

## 8.5 Auto-Responders

Reuse the existing AR01–AR10 auto-responder framework.

Permit only authorized, low-risk, preapproved responses.

Suppress automatic responses when:

- A message concerns confidential survivor information.
- The sender requests no contact.
- The communication channel may be unsafe.
- The message appears suspicious.
- A response could create a financial or legal commitment.
- Consent or contact authorization is uncertain.

